WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:07.025
First: why does the program read each
provider's A P I instead of its email?

3
00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:08.064
The answer is b.

4
00:00:08.064 --> 00:00:10.922
Email reaches a person who may have left,

5
00:00:10.922 --> 00:00:14.300
carries no owner or due
date, and can be imitated.

6
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:19.313
The provider's own record is the source of
truth, and email stays an early warning.

7
00:00:19.313 --> 00:00:23.299
Second: the Azure retirement's
action basis starts with rule.

8
00:00:23.299 --> 00:00:24.400
What does that mean?

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.625
The answer is b.

10
00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:29.176
The kit inferred that action
is required by a stated rule,

11
00:00:29.176 --> 00:00:32.425
because Azure has no field
the kit reads that says so.

12
00:00:32.425 --> 00:00:34.470
Microsoft didn't set that date;

13
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.725
the kit's rule took the advisory's
end time, and the record says so.

14
00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:41.152
The module page has three more questions,

15
00:00:41.152 --> 00:00:43.700
each linked to the
section that answers it.
